#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / AppArmor Specification
PACKAGE: apparmor
LANGUAGE: C, policy language, packaging
STATUS: W2
ROLE: Mandatory application/service access-control policy

## PROGRAM
AppArmor constrains application behavior through named security profiles governing filesystem, capability, and related access.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream AppArmor / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: application -> profile mediation -> kernel enforcement -> audit evidence
WHITE_EDITION: profile and policy overlay
GUI: JavaFX applications receive profiles only where a meaningful security boundary exists

## SPEC
- least privilege
- explicit profile ownership
- no broad exceptions solely to make an application work
- distinguish complain and enforce modes
- document material permissions

## QUALITY
TEST: parse/load, enforcement, denied operations, transitions, audit logs, update/rollback
ECONOMY: profile complexity and material policy overhead

## SOURCE POLICY
Prefer profiles, packaging, and policy. Native C changes require a concrete enforcement/correctness requirement and regression evidence.
